# libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects `/` to the public `/discover` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only `/login` binds the SSO directive (see the note in [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga's SSO button. Taiga's AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local `test-login-oidc.js` and `test-login-native.js` specs, which enter at `/login` and log out through Taiga's own control."
msgstr "Taiga resendas `/` al publiko `/discover` ekspozicias, kiu igas nudan Login ligon sed ne la OIDC-enirpunkton; nur `/login` ligas la SSO direktivon (Vidu la noton en [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js))La komunaj roluloj ĉiam eniras ĉe la retejo radiko, do ili neniam povas atingi TaigaSSO-butono. AngularJS-ŝelo de Taiga ankaŭ eksponas logoon nur tra `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` direktivoj, kiujn la senmarka en-app logout-helpanto ne povas aktivigi. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) Tial deklaras `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` kaj `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; La ekvivalentaj vojaĝoj estas movitaj per la rol-lokaj `test-login-oidc.js` kaj `test-login-native.js` Specoj, kiuj eniras ĉe `/login` kaj elsalutas tra Taigapropra kontrolo."

# libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects ``/`` to the public ``/discover`` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only ``/login`` binds the SSO directive (see the note in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` and log out through Taiga’s own control."
msgstr "Taiga resendas ``/`` al publiko ``/discover`` ekspozicias, kiu igas nudan Login ligon sed ne la OIDC-enirpunkton; nur ``/login`` ligas la SSO direktivon (Vidu la noton en ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` kaj elsalutas tra Taigapropra kontrolo."

